---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<Base
  title={`Terms of use — ${site.name}`}
  description={`The terms that apply when you use ${site.name}.`}
>
  <section class="section legal">
    <div class="wrap legal__inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="h2">Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="legal__updated mono">Applies to Serafim v{site.version} · {site.packageId}</p>

      <p class="lead">
        Keep it reasonable, keep it lawful, and keep other people welcome.
        Here is what that means in practice.
      </p>

      <h2>Your account</h2>
      <p>
        You need one account per person. Pick a username that is not
        misleading, keep control of the device you sign in from, and tell us
        if you think someone else has used your account. You are responsible
        for what is done through your account.
      </p>

      <h2>What you may not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Harass, threaten or impersonate anyone.</li>
        <li>Post illegal content, or content you do not have the right to share.</li>
        <li>Spam groups, or use the service to send bulk unsolicited messages.</li>
        <li>
          Probe, attack or disrupt the service, or try to get at accounts or
          data that are not yours.
        </li>
        <li>
          Use automated scripts to scrape profiles, harvest contact details or
          send messages on other people's behalf.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your content</h2>
      <p>
        You keep the rights to the photos, messages and voice notes you send.
        You give Serafim permission to deliver them to the people you send
        them to, and to store your text messages so they can be shown to you
        later. Chat photos and voice notes are not stored on our servers —
        they are delivered directly and kept on the recipients' devices.
      </p>

      <h2>Groups</h2>
      <p>
        Group owners and admins set the rules for their rooms. If you are
        removed from a group, that is the owner's decision and you accept it.
        Everyone in a group is responsible for what is posted inside it.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability</h2>
      <p>
        The service is provided as-is, without warranty. We aim to keep it
        running, but we do not promise that it will never be unavailable or
        that every message will always arrive. Where the app offers a
        mandatory update, that update takes priority so the app stays working.
      </p>

      <h2>Ending it</h2>
      <p>
        You can delete your account at any time, and we may suspend an
        account that breaks these terms. Deleting your account removes your
        profile, relationships and stored messages.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If these terms change, the new version will be published here and
        announced in the official SERAFIM chat inside the app.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@serafim.app">hello@serafim.app</a>,
        or open an issue on{' '}
        <a href={site.repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="legal__back">
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/">← Back to the homepage</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal__inner {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .legal__updated {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .legal :global(h2) {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }

  .legal :global(ul) {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }

  .legal :global(li) {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }

  .legal :global(p) {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }

  .legal__back {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }
</style>
